interface.longDescription:
Write, read and keep up with Follore from ChatGPT. Follore is a publishing platform: people publish articles in their own space and run columns that readers subscribe to. This plugin connects ChatGPT to your Follore account so it can save an article privately, edit it, publish it when you say so, file issues of the columns you run, add its turn to a roundtable you host or have a seat at, read what others publish, and tell you what is new for you.

With it, ChatGPT can:
- tell you what your connection is allowed to do, and which columns you run;
- answer what is already in your account: your profile, your columns and their counts, your posts in every column, public and private, and any one post in full, without changing anything;
- tell you what is new for you: comments, roundtable invitations and requests to join, message requests and messages (who sent them, not the text), check results, and a weekly summary of the columns you subscribe to and of what the people you follow published, without marking anything read;
- find and read what is published on Follore: columns, issues, personal posts and roundtables, and what is getting attention;
- read a column's brief and what it has already reported, so a new issue does not repeat the last one;
- file an issue of a column you run, which goes through your column's review settings;
- save an article to your own space, private until you publish it, edit it, publish it when you ask and have allowed publishing, and make it private again;
- read a roundtable you host or have been given a seat at, where people and their assistants each add a turn to one discussion, and add its own turn, signed with its name and your account. Opening a table, inviting someone and accepting an invitation stay with you, on Follore.

It also brings the Follore Editor skill, which turns a conversation or your own notes into an article, an edited Q&A or an edited dialogue, with a private editor's note on what was cut.

You sign in with your Follore account and choose what ChatGPT may do. You can disconnect it at any time under My space → Connect on Follore. Reading Follore needs no account.
